# Copy to .env or .env.local (both gitignored) and fill in what you need. The
# omniglass binary loads .env, then .env.local over it, from the directory it
# runs in; a variable already set in your shell wins over both.

# --- Tests ------------------------------------------------------------------
# The live model test, TestOpenAILive (internal/assistant/provider), and only
# that test: the server does not read these. It skips while the key is empty.
# Base URL and model default to the install's (OpenRouter) when unset; these
# values point it at Bedrock's gpt-oss, which takes a Bedrock API key.
OMNIGLASS_TEST_MODEL_KEY=
OMNIGLASS_TEST_MODEL_BASE_URL=https://bedrock-runtime.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/openai/v1
OMNIGLASS_TEST_MODEL_NAME=openai.gpt-oss-20b-1:0

# --- Server -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Settings by environment (#2223): any key Admin > Settings shows, as
# OMNIGLASS_SETTING__<NAMESPACE>__<KEY>=value (double underscore between the
# parts). The env level sits between the settings file and the console
# binding, so an admin's edit still wins; a profile-domain namespace (ui,
# keybindings) is refused at boot.
#
# Platform secrets by environment (#2223): OMNIGLASS_SECRET__<NAME> declares
# the platform secret <name> (lowercased, each _ a -), its value one JSON
# object {"type": "<secret type>", "fields": {...}} in single quotes. Held in
# the server's memory, never stored; a setting names it like any secret.
#
# omnibot on Amazon Bedrock's OpenAI-compatible endpoint is these five.
# Uncomment them, put a Bedrock API key in the last, and `omniglass lab run`
# (which forwards every OMNIGLASS_SETTING__ and OMNIGLASS_SECRET__ variable to
# its server) runs omnibot on Bedrock with no further command.
# OMNIGLASS_SETTING__ASSISTANT__PROVIDER=openai
# OMNIGLASS_SETTING__ASSISTANT__BASE_URL=https://bedrock-runtime.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/openai/v1
# OMNIGLASS_SETTING__ASSISTANT__MODEL=openai.gpt-oss-20b-1:0
# OMNIGLASS_SETTING__ASSISTANT__KEY_SECRET=bedrock-key
# OMNIGLASS_SECRET__BEDROCK_KEY='{"type":"api-key","fields":{"key":""}}'
#
# Other examples:
#   OMNIGLASS_SETTING__RETENTION__METRIC_DAYS=30
#   OMNIGLASS_SETTING__LABEL__ACRONYMS=AV,DSP,HDMI,PoE,UC
#
# The full list of settable keys is the generated env-var reference
# (docs/src/generated/config.json; the Container image guide's Configuration
# section).
